{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508539-have-you-created-revenant-families-for-the-clans","id":1508539,"title":"Have you created revenant families for the clans?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-04-16T10:23:19-07:00","id":1508539,"title":"Have you created revenant families for the clans?","content":"It\u2019s just an interesting notion that only the Tzismce only created several and no other clans did.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-16T11:14:05-07:00","id":1508545,"title":"","content":"Probably the mad scientist thing they've got going. <br /> I like revenants to be very rare, fucked up things that most of vampiredom doesn't even realise exists. It's definitely not something every single clan is going to be involved in.<br /> <br /> There's also the question of how to make them, seeing as blood magic seems to be involved, cutting out most of the clans anyway. <br /> They're a rather involved investment that suit best the clans who are invested in playing patron/patriarch/matriarch to a living flesh and blood clan of unstable monsters. KotEK or something about the Laibon apparently suggests that using sorcery to sire a dhampir is one way to get revenant grandkids, so it definitely seems to be a family thing.<br /> <br /> I can see the <b>Tremere</b> and the <b>Sorcerer caste</b> making a handful, just as an experiment to examine the properties and limits of the Blood and blah but there's only a handful of them left and they're on the verge of extinction now that the experiment is over (so I'd tweak the backstories of the Ducheski and the Brotherhood). In my WoD even the Tzimisce lineages are falling by the wayside in the modern nights, propped up only by old clan traditionalists and Sabbat who find them more palatable than regular ghouls.<br /> <br /> I'd give the <b>Setites</b> a revenant lineage, now that I think about it. Servants and descendants of the Dark God, born with his blood in their veins, raised by his priests to be loyal and uncorrupted by the influence of the Aeons. They'll be raised alongside regular mortal children, who were either born to mortal cult members or, ah, liberated from their Aeon-enslaved parents by the Followers. Like serpentine chatterlings.<br /> Disciplines: Serpentis, Obfuscate<br /> Weakness: A part I can't decide on. Something to reflect their... moral upbringing. They'd have been raised on the Path of Typhon-Set, so a humanity or conscience malus wouldn't really work. Hmm...<br /> <br /> But just by dint of the <i>family</i> part of the equation, my first instinct is to associate them with the <b>Giovanni</b> more than any other clan. I decided to take the &quot;7 in 10* members of the living Family are ghouls&quot; (*75%) thing from the (first?) clanbook at face value and make that 75% revenants, not just the Rossilini of V20. Practicality and realism be buggered, I like my bullshit magical vampire eugenics driven family cult politics.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-16T14:43:53-07:00","id":1508564,"title":"","content":"I tend to default to the game's early canon, so Revenants are a result of (proto-)Verbena experimentation with vitae in the True Black Hand (I believe that was around 700 BC). So they are a creation of a sect, not a clan. And the secret to doing so has long been lost, and it is highly unlikely it will ever be discovered again.<br /> <br /> The famous Revenant families of the Tzimisce are a result of either 1) some families escaping control of the True Black Hand and coming under the control of one or more important Tzimisce, or 2) a renegade Tzimisce from the True Black Hand conducted his own experiments that resulted in those families before he became destroyed (by the TBH or someone else). It is probably irrelevant in most chronicles of whatever time period of the actual truth of how the Tzimisce had so many, but if I had to decide for my own chronicles it'd probably be the second option.<br /> <br /> In any case, Revenants simply don't just &quot;happen&quot; because you've polluted a mortal family long enough with ghouling. That might result in some bad things for that family, but it won't ever be Revenants.<br /> <br /> My personal taste is that I think Revenants are cool, but they are like a very heavy spice - no matter how much you may like them, they are best used sparingly and not with everything. The fewer the Revenants the better. I think the latter editions who introduced even more Revenants are overdoing it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-16T18:18:23-07:00","id":1508595,"title":"","content":"I once introduced an attempt by the Sabbat Lasombra to create a Revenant family. The attempt failed because they lacked blood magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-17T00:25:36-07:00","id":1508614,"title":"","content":"I haven't done this although for a potential Dark Ages game I did convert the revenant families into Tzimisce bloodlines. The reason is that I can't see what revenants bring but sheer shock value, and I don't need any more of that. In particular not with the Tzimisce.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-17T02:38:02-07:00","id":1508623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508539-have-you-created-revenant-families-for-the-clans?p=1508564#post1508564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I tend to default to the game's early canon, so Revenants are a result of (proto-)Verbena experimentation with vitae in the True Black Hand (I believe that was around 700 BC). So they are a creation of a sect, not a clan. And the secret to doing so has long been lost, and it is highly unlikely it will ever be discovered again.<br /> <br /> The famous Revenant families of the Tzimisce are a result of either 1) some families escaping control of the True Black Hand and coming under the control of one or more important Tzimisce, or 2) a renegade Tzimisce from the True Black Hand conducted his own experiments that resulted in those families before he became destroyed (by the TBH or someone else). It is probably irrelevant in most chronicles of whatever time period of the actual truth of how the Tzimisce had so many, but if I had to decide for my own chronicles it'd probably be the second option.<br /> <br /> In any case, Revenants simply don't just &quot;happen&quot; because you've polluted a mortal family long enough with ghouling. That might result in some bad things for that family, but it won't ever be Revenants.<br /> <br /> My personal taste is that I think Revenants are cool, but they are like a very heavy spice - no matter how much you may like them, they are best used sparingly and not with everything. The fewer the Revenants the better. I think the latter editions who introduced even more Revenants are overdoing it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sometimes it's uncanny how accurately <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a> nails the style, feel, and themes that make me like this game...<br /> <br /> I'm in 100% agreement about the rarity and origins of revenants. The latter is more of that cross-splat material that some (even many?) people dislike about the early game, but as far as the &quot;deep lore&quot; of the setting is concerned, I've always enjoyed cross-pollination between <i>Vampire, Werewolf, Mage,</i> and the rest. I don't enjoy mixing the game lines in actual play or in any kind of active &quot;metaplot&quot; -- the most egregious example being the chain of events in the Revised era that culminated in the spirit-nuking and orbital-mirror-lasering of the Ravnos Antediluvian. But as far as background material set in the (distant or recent) past is concerned? I think crossovers are not just acceptable, they're even desirable. To my mind, they definitely enrich the overall setting and make it more fun to engage with it both in actual play and outside of sessions, such as in forum discussions like these.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-17T11:16:03-07:00","id":1508653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508539-have-you-created-revenant-families-for-the-clans#post1508539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It\u2019s just an interesting notion that only the Tzismce only created several and no other clans did.</div> </div> </div> </div>It might just seem like this if you read the description and paragraphs about Revenants from a perspective that includes the Sabbat, or Tzimisce Vampires and Ghouls, with a focus and a priority. <br /> <br /> In many books and supplements there are sections describing Revenant Families - or groups, or organizations - who are involved with for example Vampires ( and other magical beings and supernatural persons ) from the Tal'Mahe'Ra, or who are friends with for example Giovanni Vampires.<br /> It is certainly curious and noteworthy to consider the different powers, attitudes, appearances, styles, and methods developed and used by the varied Revenant ( or vampiric or supernatural ) teams and groups.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-17T11:57:44-07:00","id":1508660,"title":"","content":"<b>D'habi:</b> An ancient revenant family owned by the Baali bloodline - no comment here, demon worshippers<br /> <b>Enrathi:</b> A bloodline associated with the True Black Hand, infamous for abducting and training chatterlings (Chatterlings were mortal humans, abducted as children by the True Black Hand to be trained as servants and ghouls until they are deemed worthy of being Embraced.)<br /> <b>Kairouan Brotherhood: </b>A family created through experiments of Assamite Sorcerers<br /> <b>Katayama: </b>The youngest of the revenant families. the creation of Dr. Douglas Netchurch and his childe Dr. Nancy Reage.<br /> <b>Keskinen:</b> A revenant family that serves the ancient Malkavian Louhi.<br /> <b>Marijava: </b>A bloodline associated with the True Black Hand. While they are trained as thieves and assassins, their primary function is as spies.<br /> <b>Rafastio: </b>They are witches, sorcerers, and seers loosely affiliated with the True Black Hand. They primarily act as the sect's liaisons to the Verbena tradition. Most of the members study Magick and a few are actual Awakened mages.<br /> <b>Servants of Anushin-Rawan:</b> Debased fisher-folk who served an eccentric Ventrue in early modern Greece.<br /> <b>Rosselini:</b> The Rosselini family were once mortal necromancers that crossed paths with the Giovanni. Being &quot;persuaded&quot; to become a part of the family, the Rosselinis underwent an unknown necromantic ritual to be transformed into Revenants<br /> <b>Ducheski: </b>A family formerly named Krevcheski and owned by the Tzimisce that now serves the Tremere, they are known for their skill at magic and at making mechanical devices, particularly implements of torture. Many Tremere have the Ducheski maintain their libraries and laboratories.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-17T14:38:06-07:00","id":1508669,"title":"","content":"The one clan that seems to absolutely call out for a Revenant bloodline is the Nosferatu. They live in the sewers and storm drains of major cities which even in our world has multi-generational homeless communities.<br /> <br /> An entire bloodline which has never known things like school, taxes, or technology. Depending on how deep the tunnel systems go or if the Nosferatu expanded them deeper than mortals planned, then you could be looking at something like the Troglodytes from the movie &quot;The Descent&quot;. Nosferatu vitae already mutates animals who drink from the spawning pools, and to a limited extent it mutates the ghouls to be unsightly, so what sort of monstrosity would a revenant line look like?<br /> <br /> The fascinating thing about a Nosferatu revenant line is that since the homeless community is arguably more masquerade proof, the Revenants could actually become a mole people nobility caste of sorts amongst the homeless. Then again considering the isolation involved, I am not sure I want to think about the breeding programs required to produce such a setup.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-18T09:03:37-07:00","id":1508756,"title":"","content":"I must admit, I shamelessly &quot;borrowed&quot;, SCP-3288, the Aristocrats idea a Ventrue Ravenant family<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bR_MUbkTsoQ\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bR_MUbkTsoQ\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bR_MUbkTsoQ </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bR_MUbkTsoQ\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bR_MUbkTsoQ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-19T08:35:58-07:00","id":1508894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508539-have-you-created-revenant-families-for-the-clans?p=1508660#post1508660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Ducheski: </b>A family formerly named Krevcheski and owned by the Tzimisce that now serves the Tremere, they are known for their skill at magic and at making mechanical devices, particularly implements of torture. Many Tremere have the Ducheski maintain their libraries and laboratories.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>It is an interesting question about how proficient and skilled the Ducheski Revenants are at Thaumaturgy, and how extensively there are included in the Tremere Hierarchy and in groups, teams, and establishments lead, organized, and advised by Tremere Kindred.<br /> <br /> I assume that the average - reasonable, friendly, polite, wise, and intelligent - Tremere Vampiress is distinctly willing to team up and work with Ducheski Revenants, and definitely knows how to succesfully achieve this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-19T10:30:41-07:00","id":1508907,"title":"","content":"IIRC Ducheski characters can pick Thaumaturgy as a starting discipline. I recall reading somewhere that the D'habi and Rafastio more or less defected from their respective parent organizations and are doing their own thing. Well, in case of the Rafastio, they pretty much got nuked out of a job. I could see them keeping in touch with the similarly disenfranchised Nagaraja, actually.<br /> <br /> The absence of a Setite revenant line strikes me as curious in hindsight, when even the Malks get one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-19T18:42:06-07:00","id":1508963,"title":"","content":"I generally prefer just to stick with the four originals (and the rarer than hen's teeth fifth family that defected to the Tremere), and have them being the result of Tzimisce experiments involving Vicissitude (and possible Koldunic witchcraft), which is why other clans can't replicate it. But they're just these rare things that pop up in out of the way places, like Texas Chainsaw Massacre or The Addams Family.<br /> <br /> That said, a few years ago I and some friends tried to work out a setting with just six or seven clans, folding the latter additions into the originals where possible. And as part of that we gave each a servant family. I can't recall what went were. I think the Hostwicks (from Requiem's Invictus book) went to the Ventrue. The Gangrel one was the Bratovitch. I can't recall the others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-20T03:13:13-07:00","id":1509015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508539-have-you-created-revenant-families-for-the-clans?p=1508907#post1508907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IIRC Ducheski characters can pick Thaumaturgy as a starting discipline.</div> </div> </div> </div>Being on team and in faction with the Tremere / with Warlocks certainly has some definite advantages and benefits. It is curious for me whether the Ducheski Revenants also have a role and take part in regard directly securing and developing Tremere Chantries. <br /> <br /> It has to be noted that certainly this Revenant Family has interests, methods, and projects other than supporting Tremere Vampires. Though from what I have read about them they do seem very exclusive and focused on their preferred areas, fields, capabilities, and activities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 04-20-2023, 06:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-20T09:07:15-07:00","id":1509041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508539-have-you-created-revenant-families-for-the-clans?p=1508907#post1508907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IIRC Ducheski characters can pick Thaumaturgy as a starting discipline. I recall reading somewhere that the D'habi and Rafastio more or less defected from their respective parent organizations and are doing their own thing. Well, in case of the Rafastio, they pretty much got nuked out of a job. I could see them keeping in touch with the similarly disenfranchised Nagaraja, actually.<br /> <br /> The absence of a Setite revenant line strikes me as curious in hindsight, when even the Malks get one.</div> </div> </div> </div>It certainly is a curious notion as there clan would love the idea of a revenant family to assist in their duties of serving Set.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-20T11:05:48-07:00","id":1509068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508539-have-you-created-revenant-families-for-the-clans?p=1508907#post1508907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The absence of a Setite revenant line strikes me as curious in hindsight, when even the Malks get one.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Okay, it took me some time, but found one<br /> <b>VTM: Kindred of the Ebony Kingdom, p. 15<br /> Zhenga</b> is a Setite who operates in the criminal underworld of Mombasa.<br /> <u><b>Biography:</b></u> Slaves, drugs, vitae, and secrets are all hers and for anyone to buy \u2013 for the right price. Standing on good ground with the native Laibon, Zhenga prepares to claim Mombasa as her official domain to serve as a beachhead for Setite operations in sub-Saharan Africa. <b>She is also trying to create a new revenant line called <i>bima</i></b> (the Nilote word for ghoul), obedient only to the Setites in the African wilderness. The &quot;bima project&quot; has enjoyed some few successes and the resulting revenants are dark and hairy, with long canine teeth and thick, clawlike fingernails.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-20T14:25:20-07:00","id":1509097,"title":"","content":"Still the fact that the Followers of Set don't have a couple of revenant lines is curious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-20T15:37:51-07:00","id":1509109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508539-have-you-created-revenant-families-for-the-clans?p=1509068#post1509068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Okay, it took me some time, but found one<br /> <b>VTM: Kindred of the Ebony Kingdom, p. 15<br /> Zhenga</b> is a Setite who operates in the criminal underworld of Mombasa.<br /> <u><b>Biography:</b></u> Slaves, drugs, vitae, and secrets are all hers and for anyone to buy \u2013 for the right price. Standing on good ground with the native Laibon, Zhenga prepares to claim Mombasa as her official domain to serve as a beachhead for Setite operations in sub-Saharan Africa. <b>She is also trying to create a new revenant line called <i>bima</i></b> (the Nilote word for ghoul), obedient only to the Setites in the African wilderness. The &quot;bima project&quot; has enjoyed some few successes and the resulting revenants are dark and hairy, with long canine teeth and thick, clawlike fingernails.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow, kudos for digging that up! The first I hear about Laibon revenants, too.<br /> This reads like it's a relatively recent attempt.. you would think they would have dabbled with it way earlier, but maybe they prefer Ushabti or necromantic constructs. Well, I have my private headcanon about the feline Bubasti kinfolk. Still, there are some historic connections between Egypt and Nubia that gives me a few ideas for a potential for a revenant story.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-20T16:43:27-07:00","id":1509114,"title":"","content":"The Giovanni don't have Revenants?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-21T00:42:17-07:00","id":1509145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508539-have-you-created-revenant-families-for-the-clans?p=1509114#post1509114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Giovanni don't have Revenants?</div> </div> </div> </div>20th edition had the Rosselini family as the Giovanni revenants, and mentioned that there are ongoing attempts to breed them into the other families to create more too.<br /> <br /> Outside of that, no.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-21T00:50:12-07:00","id":1509147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508539-have-you-created-revenant-families-for-the-clans?p=1509114#post1509114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Giovanni don't have Revenants?</div> </div> </div> </div>There are certainly Revenant families, guilds, organisations, and groups associated and related to Giovanni Kindred. This does includes Revenants who are followers, allies, supporters, and friends of Giovanni Vampiresses and Vampires who come from the more specialized and recent teams and groups of Clan Giovanni.<br /> For example / for instance the Pisanob, the Dunsirn, and the Milliner Giovanni Vampires might be cooperating and involved with Vampiric persons who definitely are Revenants, and who are distinctly related to them and involved with them.<br /> <br /> It has to be noted and emphasized that Clan Giovanni has a long, interesting, curious, and complex past / history of involving many additional beings and persons ( including of course definitely Wraiths / Ghosts ) on some distinct level. There are various social phenomenon and particular events which characterize the interactions between Giovanni Kindred and the other citizens, fellows, beings, and persons who are involved with these Vampires and their organisations, guilds, and establishments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-01T22:48:19-07:00","id":1533469,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ve made the Dunsirn family into Revenants, whose family weakness is that they have to consume human flesh in order to restore their blood points.<br /> <br /> I really like Revenants, though I do feel that thematically they should be consolidated. By which I mean there should be one source of Revenants instead of arising from a lot of different sources. As it is now, there are the Tzimisce Revenants, Black Hand Revenants, and the miscellaneous ones. <br /> <br /> I\u2019m not sure what source I would go with, any one would require changing or eliminating Revenant families that I like. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-02T00:56:06-07:00","id":1533473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508539-have-you-created-revenant-families-for-the-clans?p=1533469#post1533469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really like Revenants, though I do feel that thematically they should be consolidated. By which I mean there should be one source of Revenants instead of arising from a lot of different sources. As it is now, there are the Tzimisce Revenants, Black Hand Revenants, and the miscellaneous ones.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m not sure what source I would go with, any one would require changing or eliminating Revenant families that I like.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, and the source should be the Tzimisce. They had them first and they were splendid and now we\u2019re talking about everyone and their ghouled cat having revenants. I dare say that even a few Black Hand revenant families could stay through Old Clan Tzimisce.<br /> <br /> Although to be honest, I never read Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand, so I have no idea what OCT\u2019s relationship the rest of the True Black Hand is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-02T10:52:09-07:00","id":1533494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508539-have-you-created-revenant-families-for-the-clans?p=1533473#post1533473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although to be honest, I never read Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand, so I have no idea what OCT\u2019s relationship the rest of the True Black Hand is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some individual vampires of the Old Clan Tzimisce are members of the True Black Hand, but not all are. It's hard to tell because all we know are that there are very few members of the Old Clan Tzimisce, but there are also very few members of the True Black Hand. <br /> <br /> The True Black Hand had less than 200 members, and once you eliminate those members who have infiltrated the Sabbat and Camarilla, the others only number 50 or so. Once you factor in all the clans who are members, there may be only a half dozen or so members of the Old Tzimisce in the True Black Hand. DSotBH does not give any potential numbers for the Old Clan Tzimisce in total, but it's likely much greater than a half dozen. But everywhere they are mentioned, it's always as being few in number, and they simply seem to be an acceptable source of new recruits, not some bulwark of the TBH.<br /> <br /> It's not until the Tzimisce Clanbook that we get more information about the Old Clan, but here again their numbers are always described as few. The only real new information we get is that some of them have organized the Oradea League for mutual protection.<br /> <br /> So for my chronicles, I'd probably say there are several dozen Old Clan Tzimisce at most, mainly around old Transylvania (now in Romania) so that they are close enough to support one another in the League. Organized into a very small broods of one elder vampire and a few blood-bonded childer (or possibly grand-childer if they allowed a favorite childe to sire). Some of these broods could be elsewhere than Transylvania. Only a small number of the elders are secret members of the TBH, and they might have been members even before the Anarch Revolt. But other STs will do their own things in their own chronicles.<br /> <br /> Of course, much of the assumptions that existed in old VtM sourcebooks and the original conception of the setting have long been dropped. New developers and writers did whatever they wanted with existing concepts. So while talking about the canon of this edition or that edition can be fun and help people figure out what they want to do in their own chronicles, it's also immaterial.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-02T12:23:31-07:00","id":1533498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508539-have-you-created-revenant-families-for-the-clans?p=1533469#post1533469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really like Revenants, though I do feel that thematically they should be consolidated. By which I mean there should be one source of Revenants instead of arising from a lot of different sources.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508539-have-you-created-revenant-families-for-the-clans?p=1533473#post1533473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, and the source should be the Tzimisce.</div> </div> </div> </div>If we go by Stoker characters, Revenants for me were Renfield, while ghouls would be closer to those who fell under Dracula's spell - Lucy, Mina. The Tzimisce - and especially the Old Clan - are the best fit because they complete the setting with being Stoker Draculas.<br /> That said, limiting Revenants to one Clan would be a waste of story potential, imo. They are essentially half-vampires (Dhampirs straight up copied the mechanics), and that concept is more universal than just a 'Renfield'. The classic <i>gh\u016bl</i>\u200b of arabic folklore for example comes to mind, and I have considered the <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Amkhat_(MTR)\" target=\"_blank\">Amkhat</a> as a candidate for Setite based Revenants.<br /> <br /> I can understand that together with exclusivity the concept loses some of its originality, though. That's a general thing and many people felt the same about Blood Sorcery and signature Disciplines. I generally prefer opening up good concepts for adding more character variety and options, but that kind of balance between unique attributes and player freedom is tricky to get right to everyone's satisfaction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-03T12:29:32-07:00","id":1533528,"title":"","content":"I certainly would go with the notion that each clan has a chosen family line that they follow and select the best of the best for an embrace and maybe each has a Revenant branch that best suits them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-05T05:20:06-07:00","id":1533598,"title":"","content":"Are the Revenant families from the Tal'Mahe'Ra associated with some specific Kindred Clan ( including Antitribu Vampires ), from this Sect ? Or do they also distinctly are associated with the Tzimisce ? The Old Clan Tzimisce are in the Black Hand Sect, so the chance and the possibilities are there.<br /> These Revenant Families seem rather different from the Sabbat Revenants ( Obertus, Zantosas and others ) so I am wandering considerably about this issue and question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-05T07:05:06-07:00","id":1533602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508539-have-you-created-revenant-families-for-the-clans?p=1533598#post1533598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are the Revenant families from the Tal'Mahe'Ra associated with some specific Kindred Clan ( including Antitribu Vampires ), from this Sect ? Or do they also distinctly are associated with the Tzimisce ? The Old Clan Tzimisce are in the Black Hand Sect, so the chance and the possibilities are there.<br /> These Revenant Families seem rather different from the Sabbat Revenants ( Obertus, Zantosas and others ) so I am wandering considerably about this issue and question.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Dirty Secrets </i>noted the origin of the Tal'Mahe'Ra Revenants as - drumroll - the Verbena somehow being experts on vitae and creating Revenants with Magick. That includes the Tzimisce lines. Those were later (soft-)retconned to be the result of breeding, but the True Black Hand lines never got the same treatment for their origins. V20 is careful and gives nothing definite on it either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-05T07:45:26-07:00","id":1535171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508539-have-you-created-revenant-families-for-the-clans?p=1508623#post1508623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sometimes it's uncanny how accurately <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a> nails the style, feel, and themes that make me like this game...<br /> <br /> I'm in 100% agreement about the rarity and origins of revenants. The latter is more of that cross-splat material that some (even many?) people dislike about the early game, but as far as the &quot;deep lore&quot; of the setting is concerned, I've always enjoyed cross-pollination between <i>Vampire, Werewolf, Mage,</i> and the rest. I don't enjoy mixing the game lines in actual play or in any kind of active &quot;metaplot&quot; -- the most egregious example being the chain of events in the Revised era that culminated in the spirit-nuking and orbital-mirror-lasering of the Ravnos Antediluvian. But as far as background material set in the (distant or recent) past is concerned? I think crossovers are not just acceptable, they're even desirable. To my mind, they definitely enrich the overall setting and make it more fun to engage with it both in actual play and outside of sessions, such as in forum discussions like these.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand to a degree but I much rather they continue weaving all of them together, to not do so is like pretending that these games don't happen within the same world, and at that point it shouldn't becalled the World of Darkness but Games of Darkness as not to be misleading, also loved everything that happened with the Ravnos it's one of the few things that they did almost entirely right in the transition to V5 the only thing that gets close is the Hecata","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28212-jackjk","name":"JackJK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-05T13:05:06-07:00","id":1535182,"title":"","content":"Since Ventrue have the feeding restriction and are all aristocratic twats, I've always thought they should be blood farmers (more like blood barons).<br /> So I created a bloodline of Ventrue whose business is that. Since the fall of rome.<br /> <br /> And, at a certain moment, they would've developed a revenant lineage, whose blood supersedes the feeding restriction (like vampiric vitae does). Which would solidify them as the providers for the most basic needs of the Ventrue clan.<br /> I still think revenants should be rare, even between Tzimisces. So not all clans have, neither all bloodlines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-07T21:50:10-07:00","id":1536922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1508539-have-you-created-revenant-families-for-the-clans#post1508539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It\u2019s just an interesting notion that only the Tzismce only created several and no other clans did.</div> </div> </div> </div>I assume the Cappadocians did, to tend to the all of the bodies of their victims. It's where the Giovanni learned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25666,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25666-illuminostro","user":"Illuminostro","date":". 06-08-2024, 01:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25666-illuminostro","name":"Illuminostro","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}